.TH CTI-TRIAGE 1 "2026-11-18" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-triage \- turn one threat-intel advisory into facts from our own tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-triage
.BR \-\-show\-input " | " \-\-read " | " \-\-facts
.B \-\-message
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-sender
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-subjects\-file
.IR F ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR D ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-triage \-\-facts \-\-message
.I advisory.txt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-triage
is advisory triage run by hand (phase 3 of the triage redesign). It reads
one advisory, a text file holding its body, and writes nothing.
.PP
A model, the
.IR reader ,
is started with no tools, no MCP servers and no session file, and is shown
the advisory alone. It never sees the organisation's data. It answers with
the vendors, products, versions and ATT&CK techniques the advisory concerns.
Code then removes every claim the advisory does not support: a product,
vendor or fixed version not in the advisory text, a quote not in it word
for word, a technique that is not an ATT&CK ID. Techniques the reader added
that the advisory does not name are marked as inferred.
.PP
.B \-\-facts
then looks the rest up in Falcon: which installed applications match each
product, with host counts and about how many run a version older than the
fixed one; how many hosts saw each indicator (the domains, IPs and hashes
code extracted, and the hosts of defanged links); and how many Falcon alerts
named each technique in the last 30 days. Every value is re-checked for its
exact shape before it goes into a query, and lookups are capped per
advisory: 5 products, 25 indicators, 10 techniques.
.PP
Every model call's tokens and cost are printed on stderr.
.SH OPTIONS
Exactly one of
.BR \-\-show\-input ,
.B \-\-read
or
.B \-\-facts
is required.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-input
Print what the reader would be shown. No model call, no lookups.
.TP
.B \-\-read
Run the reader and print its answer after the checks, with what was removed.
.TP
.B \-\-facts
Run the reader, then the Falcon lookups, and print the fact sheet.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " FILE"
The advisory's body, up to 256 KiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " S"
.TQ
.BI \-\-sender " S"
Header lines for the reader, if known.
.TP
.BI \-\-subjects\-file " F"
With
.BR \-\-facts :
use a saved reader answer instead of a model call.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON
.RB ( cti\-subjects/1
or
.BR cti\-facts/1 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " D"
Give up after this long. Default: 5m.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TRIAGE_MODEL
The reader's model: an alias or a full id. Required for a model call.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_BIN
The claude CLI, if it is not on the path.
.TP
.B TRIAGE_READER_INSTRUCTIONS
The reader's instructions. Default:
.IR $FLEET_CODE/agents/triage-reader/CLAUDE.md .
.TP
.B TRIAGE_BLIND_SPOTS
What Falcon cannot see, repeated on every fact sheet.
.TP
.BR FALCON_BASE_URL ", " FALCON_CLIENT_ID ", " FALCON_CLIENT_SECRET
As for
.BR cti\-falcon (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done. A lookup that failed is shown on the sheet, not in the exit status.
.TP
.B 1
The advisory, the instructions or the reader's answer could not be read, the
model call failed, Falcon could not be reached, or the run timed out.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
What the reader would see:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-triage \-\-show\-input \-\-message adv.txt
.RE
.PP
The fact sheet:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-triage \-\-facts \-\-message adv.txt \-\-subject "Weekly threat roundup"
.RE
.PP
Replay a saved answer without paying for another call:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-triage \-\-read \-\-message adv.txt \-\-json > saved.json
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-triage \-\-facts \-\-message adv.txt \-\-subjects\-file saved.json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-falcon (1),
RUNBOOK.md section 11k, SECURITY.md.
